<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
    <!--
        False positive: CVE-2020-29582 affects Kotlin before 1.4.21 (incorrect default permissions in temp files).
        Every Kotlin artifact we resolve is well past that: 2.3.21 for kotlin-stdlib/-jdk7/-jdk8/-reflect,
        and 1.9.10 for the kotlin-stdlib-common straggler.
        This rule previously targeted com.fasterxml.jackson.module/jackson-module-kotlin and recorded
        "zero matches" on every scan - the CVE actually matches the org.jetbrains.kotlin coordinates.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Fixed in Kotlin 1.4.21; every Kotlin artifact we resolve is far past it. Version-agnostic by design.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2020-29582</cve>
    </suppress>
    <!--
        Not reachable, fix now available: CVE-2026-53914 (unsafe deserialization in Kotlin build-cache
        metadata, NVD 9.8) is fixed in 2.4.20, which reached GA after this rule was written (2.4.21 is current
        as of 2026-10-25). Kotlin arrives transitively via spring-ai-starter-model-openai -> kotlin-reflect
        -> kotlin-stdlib (2.3.21); this app is pure Java and never touches Kotlin's Gradle build-cache
        deserialization path, so it isn't reachable at runtime. Remove this suppression once Kotlin is
        overridden to 2.4.20+ (or Spring AI / Boot pull it in). Still required until then: without it the
        CVSS>=9.0 gate fails.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Not reachable at runtime in this pure-Java app. Fixed in Kotlin 2.4.20 (now GA); remove once Kotlin is overridden or upgraded to 2.4.20+.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
    </suppress>
    <!--
        No fix released: CVE-2026-14683 / CVE-2026-14686 (CVSS 2.0 LOW) affect HdrHistogram up to 2.2.2, which is
        the latest release as of 2026-10-25. The flaws are in decodeFromCompressedByteBuffer and
        DoubleHistogram.recordValue. HdrHistogram arrives transitively via micrometer-core, which records
        histograms from its own timer values; this app never decodes externally supplied histograms.
        Revisit if a release after 2.2.2 ships.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>No fix released (2.2.2 is latest); LOW severity; vulnerable decoding path not reachable from outside (Micrometer-internal). Revisit when HdrHistogram releases past 2.2.2.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.hdrhistogram/HdrHistogram@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-14683</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-14686</cve>
    </suppress>
    <!--
        Not reachable: CVE-2026-104721 / CVE-2026-19880 (CVSS 6.3) are path traversals where an MDC-based
        discriminator value flows into a nested FileAppender path, i.e. they require a SiftingAppender
        configuration. This app has no logback.xml and uses Spring Boot's default console logging, with no
        SiftingAppender or MDC discriminator anywhere. The fix is only in logback 1.6.5 (affected: through
        1.6.4), a new minor line Spring Boot does not yet manage. Remove once Boot moves to a fixed logback.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>Requires a SiftingAppender with an MDC discriminator; this app has no logback config and uses Boot's default console logging. Fixed only in logback 1.6.5; remove once Boot manages a fixed version.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/ch\.qos\.logback/logback-.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-104721</cve>
        <cve>CVE-2026-19880</cve>
    </suppress>
</suppressions>